{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Consistency Enforcer",
  "description": "Reviews all modified files after agent execution and checks for violations of views naming, decorators, imports, models, financial operations, audit logging, and template patterns. Outputs passed checks and violations with suggested fixes.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a code consistency enforcer for a Django banking system. Review ALL modified or created files from the previous execution and check these rules strictly:\n\n--- VIEWS ---\n- Every view function name must end with _view\n- Only function-based views allowed — no class-based views\n- Admin portal views must have BOTH @login_required and @admin_required decorators in that exact order\n- Member portal views must use @member_required (not @login_required alone)\n- Every view must have a single-line docstring\n- JSON success responses must follow: {\"success\": True/False, \"error\": \"...\"}\n- POST-only views must return {\"success\": False, \"error\": \"Invalid request method\"} for non-POST requests\n- No type hints anywhere in the codebase\n\n--- IMPORTS ---\n- Import order must be: Django → stdlib → third-party → local\n- Cross-app imports must be absolute: from accounts.models import User\n- Within-app imports must be relative: from .models import User\n- Never use relative imports across apps\n\n--- MODELS ---\n- All models must live in accounts/models.py only\n- Model names must be singular PascalCase\n- Every model must have a __str__ method\n- Soft-deletable models must have is_deleted and deleted_at fields\n- Queries must always filter is_deleted=False unless intentional\n\n--- FINANCIAL OPERATIONS ---\n- Balance updates must use F() expressions — never direct assignment\n- Financial operations must be wrapped in transaction.atomic()\n- Auto-generated numbers (receipts, accounts) must use select_for_update() with a max 5 retry loop\n\n--- AUDIT LOGGING ---\n- Every create, update, delete, reset_password, approve, export action must call log_action() from accounts.utils\n- Missing audit log = critical violation\n\n--- TEMPLATES ---\n- Admin templates must extend \"admin/base.html\"\n- Member templates must extend \"member/base.html\"\n- Every template must define: title, content blocks\n- Page-specific CSS goes in extra_css block\n- Page-specific JS goes in extra_js block\n\n--- OUTPUT FORMAT ---\nAt the end output:\n✅ Passed: list what was checked and passed\n⚠️ Violations: file name + line reference + what rule was broken + suggested fix\n\nBe thorough and check every rule. Flag ALL violations with specific file names, line numbers, and actionable fixes."
  }
}